        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'HORSE',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "HORSE is a mixed poker game format that rotates through five different poker variants in a fixed sequence. The acronym stands for Hold'em, Omaha Hi/Lo, Razz, Seven Card Stud, and Eight-or-Better (Stud Hi/Lo). Popular in major tournaments like the World Series of Poker, HORSE tests a player's versatility across multiple poker disciplines. All games are played in Fixed-Limit format.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Developed in the United States as a way to test poker players' skills across multiple variants. Became prominent in high-stakes cash games and tournament play.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '2-8 players (typically 6-8 for optimal play).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard deck, poker chips, dealer button.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Deal according to current game in rotation (Hold'em, Omaha, etc.).",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: "C.H.O.R.S.E.: Adds Crazy Pineapple (C) before Hold'em; six variants in rotation. Community and stud games are evenly split.",
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'C.H.O.R.S.E.L.: Adds Crazy Pineapple (C) and Lowball (L); seven variants. California or Ace-to-Five Lowball.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: "H.O.S.E.: Drops Razz; four variants: Hold'em, Omaha Hi/Lo, Seven-Card Stud, Stud Eight-or-Better. Shorter rotation.",
                  },
                  {
                    text: "Eight Game Mix: Eight variants: 2-7 Triple Draw, Limit Hold'em, Limit Omaha Hi-Lo, Razz, Seven-Card Stud, Stud Hi-Lo 8, No-Limit Hold'em, Pot-Limit Omaha High. Also known as T.H.O.R.S.E.H.A.",
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
